---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Donation processing software for nonprofits"
  description="Donorbox vs Zeffy vs Givebutter and more: what online donation platforms cost after platform and processing fees, and which fits your shop."
  section="donation-processing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Donation processing' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Donation processing software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Donation platforms take the money: forms, recurring gifts, and the fees
        on every gift. Genuinely free options compete head-on with paid ones
        here, so the real comparison is the fee math on your volume.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />


      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Three models compete.
        <a href="/go/zeffy" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Zeffy</a> charges
        the nonprofit nothing at all, funded by optional donor tips.
        <a href="/go/givebutter" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Givebutter</a>
        is free with tips on (0% platform fee) or a flat 3% with tips off, and
        adds events, auctions, and peer-to-peer.
        <a href="/go/donorbox" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Donorbox</a>
        charges a platform fee (about 2.95%, lower on Pro) and delivers the
        deepest recurring-gift tooling in the class: failed-card recovery, donor
        portals, and CRM integrations. WordPress shops reach for
        <a href="/go/givewp" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">GiveWP</a>, and
        <a href="/go/4agoodcause" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">4aGoodCause</a>
        offers flat monthly pricing with no transaction fees.
      </p>
      <p>
        Run your annual online volume through each fee model before choosing,
        and test the donor-facing checkout on your phone. Donor experience moves
        conversion more than a fee point does, and every platform here will let
        you try a live form for free.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="donation-processing" />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Processing stays free in <a href="/stacks/under-250k/">the grassroots
        stack</a> and <a href="/stacks/250k-1m/">the $250k-$1M stack</a>; paid
        tooling enters at <a href="/stacks/1m-5m/">$1M-$5M</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
